`pgvector` is now a required dependency rather than an optional extra, and the development database image is `pgvector/pgvector:pg17`. It cannot be optional: `TicketEmbedding` uses `VectorField`, so Django needs it at import time on every start - litellm and the MCP client are lazy because they are only ever called, and a model field is not. [ADR 0003](../decisions/0003-postgresql-with-pgvector-only.md) already made PostgreSQL-with-pgvector the only supported database, so this asks for nothing that was not already required.
